== CONTROL ==
A 20  UIP 0 DV 2 RS 0
  DV 2 is the only running setting; RS 0 disables the periodic tick
B 2  SET 0 PIE 0 AIE 0 UIE 0
  SQWE 0 DM 0 24/12 1 DSE 0
  DM 1 is BINARY counting - the MOS assumes BCD, so DM 1 alone
  would explain a year printing as 197B and an hour as F9.
  PIE with RS non-zero is a free-running IRQ nothing claims.
C 10  IRQF 0 PF 0 AF 0 UF 1
D 80  VRT 1  <- SECOND READ, IGNORE IT
  The VRT that means anything is the VRT FIRST READ line at
  the top: 0 there says backup power has been lost. Reading
  register D sets the bit, so this one always says 1.
C again after 1s 10  IRQF 0 PF 0 UF 1
  C clears when read. Anything set again is being REGENERATED.
